Falsifies `capability_manifest_note::verification::an_encoded_manifest_decodes_to_itself`.

The defect: `encode` forgets the byte that says whether a program writes while it reads its
input. The descriptor still decodes, to a manifest that differs from the one the program declared,
so the reader would grant something other than what was asked.

Expected to fail: the assertion that `decode` of the encoded manifest is the manifest again.

diff --git a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
index b61755828..e30a81925 100644
--- a/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
+++ b/crates/capability_manifest_note/src/lib.rs
@@ -387,7 +387,6 @@ pub const fn encode(m: &Manifest) -> [u8; DESCRIPTOR_BYTES] {
     } = m.input
     {
         out[INPUT] = 1;
-        out[WRITES_WHILE_READING] = writes_while_reading as u8;
     }
     out[REPORTS] = m.reports as u8;
     out[INTERRUPTIBLE] = m.interruptible as u8;
